You are working on couch-kit, a TypeScript framework for local multiplayer TV party games.

Package manager: Bun (1.4.2). Never use npm/yarn/pnpm.
Build: bun run build (core must build first)
Test: bun run test
Lint: bun run lint (Prettier formatting check + changeset header lint; there is no ESLint)
Format: bun run format
Typecheck: bun run typecheck

Monorepo: 7 packages under packages/ — core, runtime, client, display, host, cli, devtools.
core is the foundation; runtime builds next and powers authoritative hosts.
Build order: core, runtime, client, display, then host/cli/devtools.
display (@couch-kit/display) is the browser display host for the cross-network relay (RelayDisplayHost).
Relay services live outside the workspace: services/relay (single-process Bun relay, reference/self-host) and services/relay-worker (Cloudflare Workers + Durable Objects, one DO per room; what production uses). Relay tests are in services/relay/tests and run in the separate relay CI job, not via bun run test.

Key rules:
- Host is authoritative. Clients receive full state snapshots.
- createGameReducer wraps user reducers. Internal actions (__HYDRATE__, __PLAYER_JOINED__, etc.) are handled automatically.
- Player IDs are derived from session secrets via SHA-256.
- WebSocket port = HTTP port + 2 (default 8082).
- workspace:* references in package.json are resolved at publish time. Never change them.
- Every PR changing package source needs a changeset: bun run changeset
- Never edit CHANGELOG.md files directly.
- Never bundle react or react-native (peer dependencies).
